Z||000000||camon||10-20-2001||12:24 AM||||Hey All!<P>Well something else is going south I think. <P>First of all i'm not 100% sure what the problem is, all I do know is that the car makes a slight squeal (this occurs from the moment you start it until you shut it off). I noticed it a couple days ago for the first time it only happened when the car got good and warm..well now it does it all the time. It sounds kinda like a belt squeal only not as loud and it stays the same (it don't increase nor get louder as the throttle is applied....it stays constent). <BR>When driving you can't even hear it from inside the car only when I pull up to a red light or stop sign is it noticible. I tried listening to the engine and I can't pin point where the sound is coming from. Could it be and oil pump maybe???? How can I check if this is the problem?<BR>My oil pressure gauge when the car is warm while moving (doing speed limit) reads 40psi while hard on throttle about 60psi and when at idle is about 20psi (alittle above red...no warning light though) . When the engine is cold the oil pressuere is high (between 60 and 80). The number that really worries me is the 20psi while at idle (that sounds real low).  I have only had the car about a month I never really paid attention to the oil pressure gauge before now (so I don't even know if this is normal...it just sounds low to me).<P>I hope it ain't the oil pump...but I have a funny feeling it is......<BR>If it is the oil pump I quess that is a job for a garage huh?????? The Hayes manual tells you to lift the engine to get the oil pan off...and if that is the case I will need to take it to a garage because I don't have the garage nor the hoist to do it! Is there anyway to do the job (if it is the pump) without lifting the motor I haven't had the chance to crawl under the car yet to see the situation)???<P>I have a 87 GT with 109,000 miles.||||reg||1
