Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||10-20-2001||05:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by camon:<BR><B>I wish!!!!!!<P>I will try to tighten it but I don't think that is the problem....the belt seems tight!<P>Does that oil pressure sound low????</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That sounds low, but I'm not sure that maybe your problem. Get a manual oil gauge and check it. The oil sensor may be at fault. The squeal, A/C compressor bearing or clutch dragging? Front and rear bearing OK in the alternator? Water pump seeping at the front seal? Just a few things to check.||||reg||1
Z||000004||camon||10-20-2001||10:33 AM||||I will check the alternator. Will there be play in the alt. pulley if it is in fact alt. bearings?<P>Ohh yeah correction on the hayes procedure:<BR>I guess the engine doesn't need lifted I was reading the 4cyl procedure (late night last night...must have been more tired then I thought). The 6cyl. procedure  says to remove starter flywheel shield and pan bolts.<BR>So if need be I may be able to pull it into one of by bothers driveway to replace the oil pump if that it the problem. will need to look into getting a manual oil gauge...any ideas how much they run for (cost)?<P>Thanks! <p>[This message has been edited by camon (edited 10-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||camon||10-21-2001||12:13 AM||||Squeal was coming from the alternator shaft I think. Changed thermostat Monday and remember that some coolant splashed on the pulleys and belt. Well after I changed the thermostat I drove it for a while and had no ill noises. I parked it and forgot about it...Then Tuesday I noticed the sqeal. Well Today I remember the thermostat change and thought about spaying the alternator shaft with WD-40 thinking maybe coolant slashed on it and is causing the noise. Well I sprayed it and it hasn't made a peep since (fingers crossed).<P>I am gonna perform an oil change on Sunday (just got the car and don't know when it was done last...so it couldn't hurt). I'll use 10w30 and a new filter. If that doesn't correct the low pressure...I will get a manual oil pressure guage...and if it shows the same reading (low when warm at idle)....i'll change oil again with a heavier oil (10w40 or something).<P>Well later on<P>------------------<BR>Keith||||reg||1
